    "result_text": "All 70 tests pass (0 failures, 0 errors). The version-2 owner identity release is implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Identity derivation \u2014 V2 tag mixed in (every identifier changes, no V1 value reproduced):**\n- `mapper/IdentityKey.java` \u2014 SHA-256 now over `V2|telephone|email|soundex(lastName)`.\n- `function/owner/AssignHousehold.java` \u2014 householdId SHA-256 now over `V2|lastName|postcode` (still deterministic on last name + postcode, so housemates still share it).\n- `function/owner/AssignMemberId.java` \u2014 the REGION embedded in the memberId now comes from the new `mapper/RegionCode.java` (`identityRegion` \u2192 `\"V2\" + plainRegion`, e.g. `V2NSW`).\n\n**Keeping the V2 tag out of user-facing fields:**\n- `mapper/Locality.java` \u2014 no longer reads the memberId's region prefix (which is now V2-tagged); it derives the plain region directly from postcode/city. `Timezone` and `OwnerSegment` read `Locality`, so `locality` stays `NSW`, timezone stays `Australia/Sydney`, and the segment recomputes to `STANDARD_METRO`.\n\n**Response shape:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added an `OwnerIdentity` schema (memberId/identityKey/householdId), replaced the three top-level identifier fields with a nested `identity` object, and added a top-level integer `apiVersion` (2).\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` + new `mapper/OwnerIdentityMapper.java` \u2014 populate the nested `identity` object and set `apiVersion` to 2.\n\n**Audit event \u2192 schema version 2:**\n- `function/owner/OwnerCreatedEvent.java` \u2014 JSON now leads with `\"schemaVersion\":2`, still carrying the owner id and the (V2) memberId as the primary identifier.\n\nThe request fields are unchanged, and duplicate detection / soft-match still work because they compute the identityKey through the same (now V2) helper on both sides.",
