    "probe_text": "I now have the full picture. Here is everything applied on `POST /api/owners`, in execution order.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Non-admins get 403 (`AuthorizationDeniedException`).\n- The entire pipeline runs under one `transaction` governance (`govern: [ transaction ]` on every step), committing once at the end.\n\n## Validations (in order \u2014 each aborts with the noted status)\n\n1. **Idempotency replay check** (`CheckIdempotencyKey`) \u2014 reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header; if that key already maps to a still-existing owner, short-circuits and returns that owner with **200** (`IdempotentCreateReplayException`) instead of creating a duplicate. (A blank key, unseen key, or key whose owner was deleted falls through.)\n2. **Bean validation** (`@Valid` on `ValidateOwnerFields`, runs before its body) \u2014 `firstName`/`lastName`: `@NotNull`, name pattern, size 1\u201330; `city`: `@NotNull` size 1\u201380; `telephone`: `@NotNull` size 1\u201320; `address`/`addressLine1`/`addressLine2`: size limits; `postcode`: `^[0-9]{4}$` if present. Failure \u2192 **400** (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`).\n3. **Required-field check** (`ValidateOwnerFields`) \u2014 rejects blank/whitespace-only `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`, and address (checks structured `addressLine1` or flat `address`, in normalized form). Missing ones listed in **400** (`MissingOwnerFieldsException`). Publishes the validated body.\n4. **Future registration date** (`CheckRegistrationDateNotFuture`) \u2014 if a supplied `registrationDate` is after the server date \u2192 **400** (`FutureRegistrationDateException`). (Omitted or back-dated is allowed.)\n5. **Postcode-vs-city** (`ValidatePostcode`) \u2014 if postcode present and the city's region is known (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), the 4 digits must fall in range \u2192 else **400** (`InvalidPostcodeException`). Unknown region or absent postcode passes.\n6. **Email domain blocklist** (`CheckEmailDomainAllowed`) \u2014 rejects disposable domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 **400** (`DisposableEmailDomainException`). (Runs after email normalization below.)\n7. **City capacity (hard)** (`CheckOwnerCityCapacity`) \u2014 if the city already holds \u2265 **50** owners (case-insensitive, trimmed) \u2192 **409** (`CityAtCapacityException`).\n8. **Daily limit** (`CheckOwnerDailyLimit`) \u2014 if \u2265 **100** owners already registered on this request's effective business day \u2192 **429** (`DailyOwnerLimitException`).\n9. **Identity uniqueness (hard duplicate)** (`CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`) \u2014 computes `identityKey` = SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone|lowerEmail|soundex(lastName)`; if it equals any non-deleted owner's \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateIdentityException`). Soft-deleted owners are skipped.\n\n## Side-effects / mutations (in order)\n\nNote steps 5\u20137 below (telephone, email, address normalization) actually run *earlier* in the pipeline (they precede validations 6\u20139), mutating the validated body in place; grouped here as effects.\n\n- **Normalize telephone** (`NormalizeOwnerTelephone`) \u2014 rewrites `telephone` to E.164 (assumes `+61`, drops a leading `0`, strips spaces/dashes/brackets); invalid \u2192 **400** (`InvalidTelephoneException`).\n- **Normalize email** (`NormalizeOwnerEmail`) \u2014 blank \u2192 null; otherwise must match email regex (else **400** `InvalidEmailException`) and is stored lower-cased.\n- **Normalize address** (`NormalizeOwnerAddress`) \u2014 canonicalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`, composes the flat `address` (or normalizes the flat form alone).\n- **Build entity** (`BuildOwner`) \u2014 maps DTO \u2192 `Owner`; sets `registrationDate` to the effective business day (supplied-or-today, rolled forward past weekends and listed 2026 public holidays).\n- **Count namesakes** (`CountNamesakes`) \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive).\n- **Assign memberId** (`AssignMemberId`) \u2014 sets `memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (V2 region from postcode/city, fiscal year, SHA-256(telephone+lastName) hash, Luhn check digit); de-duplicated with `-<n>` suffix on collision.\n- **Assign household** (`AssignHousehold`) \u2014 sets deterministic `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256(`V2|normalizedLastName|postcode`).\n- **Flag possible duplicate** (`CheckPossibleDuplicate`) \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` to the lowest-id non-deleted owner with differing `identityKey` but matching `soundex(lastName)` + `postcode`.\n- **Save** (`SaveOwner`) \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (assigns the id).\n- **Audit log** (`AuditOwnerCreated`) \u2014 `AUDIT` logger line with id, memberId, registrationDate, membershipLevel.\n- **Welcome notification** (`EnqueueWelcomeNotification`) \u2014 `NOTIFY` logger line with id + memberId.\n- **Owner-created event** (`EmitOwnerCreatedEvent`) \u2014 structured JSON event to `AUDIT` logger, drawing a monotonic `seq` from `OwnerEventSequence`.\n- **Bulk-signup warning** (`MarkBulkSignupWarning`) \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning` = (owners registered today > **80**).\n- **City-capacity warning** (`MarkCityCapacityWarning`) \u2014 sets `capacityWarning` = (city holds 40\u201349 owners).\n- **Household size** (`CountHouseholdMembers`) \u2014 sets `householdSize` = owners sharing `householdId` (self included; 1 if none).\n- **Cap membership level** (`CapMembershipLevel`) \u2014 sets `membershipLevel` = derived level, capped at one above the max level among other household members.\n- **Record idempotency key** (`RecordIdempotencyKey`) \u2014 if a key was supplied, stores `key \u2192 owner.id` (first write wins).\n- **Respond** (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) \u2014 **201 Created**, `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, body = `OwnerDto`.\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: the doc comments claim these steps run \"before `SaveOwner` so the new owner is not counted,\" and the capacity/daily/namesake/duplicate checks all rely on `ownerRepository.findAll()` **not** yet including the new row \u2014 correct here only because the save happens later in the same uncommitted transaction."
